{"version":"0.1","documentType":"opinion","source":{"kind":"lrb_html","caseId":"2024_02083","path":"../miranda/opinions/coa/2024/2024_02083.htm","publicationStatus":"published"},"header":{"title":"People v Sims","slipOpinion":"2024 NY Slip Op 02083","officialCitation":"41 NY3d 995","court":"Court of Appeals","decisionDate":"2024-04-18"},"appearances":[],"opinions":[{"kind":"majority","author":null,"label":null,"joiners":[],"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"page_marker","text":"{**41 NY3d at 995}","citation":"41 NY3d at 995"},{"type":"text","text":" OPINION OF THE COURT"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"page_marker","text":"{**41 NY3d at 995}","citation":"41 NY3d at 995"},{"type":"text","text":" OPINION OF THE COURT"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Memorandum."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"The order of the Appellate Division should be affirmed."},{"type":"page_marker","text":"{**41 NY3d at 996}","citation":"41 NY3d at 996"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Defendant's claim that the sentencing court conducted an inadequate inquiry into his violation of plea conditions before imposing an enhanced sentence, to the degree \"readily discernible from the hearing transcript\" ("},{"type":"link","href":"../2011/2011_04769.htm","children":[{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","text":"People v Albergotti"}]},{"type":"text","text":", 17 NY3d 748"}]},{"type":"text","text":", 750 [2011]), is without merit. The court conducted an appropriate inquiry and provided defendant with an opportunity to dispute the factual basis for the alleged violation ("},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","text":"see People v Outley"}]},{"type":"text","text":", 80 NY2d 702, 713 [1993]; "},{"type":"link","href":"../2004/2004_07399.htm","children":[{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","text":"People v Valencia"}]},{"type":"text","text":", 3 NY3d 714"}]},{"type":"text","text":", 716 [2004])."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Defendant's ineffective assistance of counsel claims are more appropriately brought in a collateral or post-conviction CPL 440.10 proceeding ("},{"type":"link","href":"../2016/2016_06938.htm","children":[{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","text":"see People v Henderson"}]},{"type":"text","text":", 28 NY3d 63"}]},{"type":"text","text":", 66 [2016])."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Defendant's argument that his postplea statements to the probation officer required further inquiry by the court is without merit ("},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","text":"see People v Billingsley"}]},{"type":"text","text":", 54 NY2d 960, 961 [1981]). His contention that the court overstated his sentencing exposure is unpreserved."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Chief Judge Wilson and Judges Rivera, Garcia, Singas, Cannataro, Troutman and Halligan concur."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Order affirmed, in a memorandum."}],"provenance":{"startLine":7,"endLine":23}}]}],"footnotes":[],"disposition":{"text":"Order affirmed, in a memorandum.","provenance":{"startLine":23,"endLine":23}},"renderingHints":{"hasOfficialPageMarkers":true,"hasAppearances":false,"hasFootnotes":false,"hasSeparateOpinions":false},"debug":{"diagnostics":[]}}